app Shop
    A tiny order API. Orders are stored in SQLite; prices come from pricing.fluid.

target python

uses
    pricing.fluid for prices with tax
    sqlite database in "shop.db"

secrets
    ADMIN_TOKEN

settings
    port 8091

to place order (item: short text, amount in cents: whole number) -> the new order id
    Save the order with its price with tax, in one transaction.
    An empty item or a negative amount is refused.

to order total -> whole number
    The sum of every order's price with tax.

web
    every request must carry the header X-Admin-Token equal to ADMIN_TOKEN
    POST /orders   -> place order using "item" and "amount" from the JSON body; answer 201 with {"id": ...}
    GET  /total    -> {"total": order total}
    A refused order answers 400 with {"error": "..."}.

every 1 hour
    Print the order total.

test placing an order adds its taxed price to the total
    after placing an order for 100 cents, the order total is 118

on start
    Create the orders table with a migration, print "Shop API on port 8091", and start the web API.
